    action: "Use current authorized native tools directly; normal prompt reports are valid work reports. No runtime adapter, process fields, exported session/authorization ID, quota or slot telemetry is a launch prerequisite. Apply existing class authorization to host-constraint fallback without asking again; exact configuration is a preference unless explicitly hard. Parent reads before dispatch, child reads before work; no pre-creation child proof. Coordination-only targets=[] needs no invented binding; source work checks its actual scope/permission. Optional audit: machine-assemble HostExecutionRequest and actual arguments for `execution-host-prepare`; record raw events/reports with `execution-host-record --binding <file>` and optional `--prior`. Never request hand-filled JSON. Unknown outcomes reconcile before retry; cancel requested/accepted is not terminal. Dot selection is host-managed, not a fake model choice. Record validity, host finality and independent review differ. Persist configuration only under separate saving authority. See `specs/host-fallback-v1.md`.",
